        "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Characteristic invasiveness makes excision extremely problematic; difficult to distinguish between tumor and normal adipose tissue.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Poorly defined tumor margins—may contribute to the observed high recurrence rate after surgical excision.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "36–50% of patients have recurrence within 3–16 months, except with limb amputation for appendicular tumor.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Amputation of an affected limb is recommended only when quality of life is affected; tumor causes little inconvenience unless it interferes with movement (mechanical lameness), causes pressure-related pain, or develops in a vitally important anatomic site. However, amputation must be performed before growth of proximal extent of tumor crosses attainable surgical margin.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "External Beam Radiotherapy",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Beneficial for long-term tumor control—",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "median survival 40 months in a retrospective",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "study of 13 dogs, with only 1 dog (7.7%)",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "euthanized owing to tumor-related signs (vs.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "26.7% with surgery alone).",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dogs with measurable disease may only",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "have stabilization of the tumor.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cytoreductive surgery to microscopic",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "disease prior to radiation may result in",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "long-term disease control.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Unlikely to kill mitotically inactive mature",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "adipocytes but may inhibit progressive",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "infiltration by damaging tumor micro-",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "circulation.",
              "pdf_page": 917,
              "printed_page": 835,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "External Beam Radiotherapy"
            }
          ]
        },
